title: LoudPeopleAtChurchDoor
---
<<disable_controls "Player">>

As you make your way up the hill you hear some disturbance up the church steps
Voices overlap shouting at each other,
There is repetitive banging on the large enterence wooden doors

<<show_text "QuestTitleChurch">>

<<enable_controls "Player">>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                        CHURCH BUNKER
//------------------------------------------------------------------------
title: ChurchBunker
---
<<disable_controls "Player">>
<<show_text "ObjectiveChurchFindOut">>

<<if $haveTalkedToChurch == true>>
    From behind the door, the pastor's voice cuts through again, sharp and bitter.
	Pastor (through door): This is what happens when people stop beliving in god!
	Pastor (through door): After Soviet times I thought people would start to belive again
    There's nothing new to gain here.
<<else>>
	<<set $haveTalkedToChurch = true>>
	The church doors are closed shut from the inside
	A small group has gathered on the steps, taking turns knocking and pleading their case
	Behind the door stands the pastor who isn't willing to let anyone in
	Pastor (through door): The Church bunker is closed. 
    Pastor (through door): Budget cuts. Austerity measures.
    Pastor (through door): Besides.. thirty years from now, I imagine God is going to be working from home anyway.
	Crowd murmurs think over how mutch they have given in the past years.
    Crowd: We've donated for years…
    Crowd: We helped build this place…
    Crowd: You can't just lock us out!
	Pastor (through door): But is it enough?
	You get the feeling this situation isn't going anywhere.
    What do you do?
	<<complete_and_hide "ObjectiveChurchFindOut" 1>>
	<<show_text "ObjectiveChurchTryToGetIn">>
-> Argue with the pastor
	<<set $badPoints += 1>>
	You: Hey man can you let me in at least?
	Pastor (through door): Am I supposed to know you? 
	You: God loves all his children.
	Pastor (through door): But the children only remember God when it's convenient.
	The crowd grows tense. 
	You've made things worse by disrespected religion and making things awkward.
-> Try to calm the crowd
	<<set $goodPoints += 1>>
	You try to get everyones attention
	You: Hey chill out, let father speek, hear whats the issue
	The crowd quiets a bit. You made things better!
	You: So can you still not let us in?
	Pastor (through door): Yes, I can not.
-> Leave
	<<set $goodPoints += 0>>
This isn't moving forward so you leave
<<complete_and_hide "ObjectiveChurchTryToGetIn" 1>>
<<complete_and_hide "QuestTitleChurch" 2>>
<<complete_text "ObjectiveFindBunkerGood2" >>
<<complete_text "ObjectiveFindBunkerOkay2" >>
<<complete_text "ObjectiveFindBunkerBad1" >>
<<endif>>

<<enable_controls "Player">>
===